  "notes": "Modified cash basis village (treated as cash, as FY2023). Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p5). Fund balance roll-forward: as previously reported (830,794) + Restatement 1,115,879 (= as restated 285,085) + 683,562 - 751,539 + 64,866 - 38,318 = 243,656. Bond proceeds are printed among revenues (governmental 440,164 Street Fund; enterprise 149,836 under nonoperating revenues, Statement of Activities general revenues) so they are receipt lines. Transfers: the Total column prints net 'Transfers in (out)' 26,548 (from the Enterprise Fund, p7); recorded gross by fund column as in FY2023: transfers_in Street 64,866, transfers_out General 38,318. No beginning cash printed (no prior-year balance sheet); ending_cash = governmental funds 'Cash and cash equivalents' 76,246 and ending_investments = 'Certificates of deposit' 152,948 (p4); county treasurer cash 6,790 and restricted CDs 7,672 are separate lines. Business-type (single Enterprise Fund) from p7 (modified cash; ties to the Statement of Activities p2-3: expenses 712,275, charges 734,590, capital grants 38,318, bond proceeds 149,836, interest 3,329, transfers (26,548)): as previously reported 1,428,388 + restatement (1,115,879) = 312,509; 312,509 + 926,073 - 712,275 - 26,548 = 499,759. Enterprise 'Grant revenue' has no grantor printed: category other, detail Grants. A proprietary Statement of Cash Flows is printed (p8) but proprietary is null as in FY2023/FY2024 (modified cash basis). Capital outlay 2,692 (General Fund) has no function printed: labelled 'Capital Outlay'. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds balance sheet (p4, total 243,656 equals government-wide), business-type from p1. Detail: the only schedule is the all-funds budgetary comparison (p9, function totals only), so detail is per-fund lines from the fund statements (p5, p7), as FY2023. Read pages 1-9 of 9"
